- **Breaking change:** Removed 2017 packs. Hosts no longer receive 2017 packs in their osquery config, and performance stats for 2017 packs are no longer stored. Upgrading drops the `packs`, `pack_targets`, and `scheduled_queries` tables and logs the names of any 2017 packs it deletes. Before upgrading to Fleet 5, run `fleetctl upgrade-packs` with fleetctl 4 against your Fleet 4 server and apply the output to convert 2017 packs to reports.
- **Breaking change:** Removed `/api/v1/fleet/packs`, `/api/v1/fleet/packs/:id`, `/api/v1/fleet/packs/id/:id`, `/api/v1/fleet/packs/:id/scheduled`, `/api/v1/fleet/packs/schedule`, `/api/v1/fleet/packs/schedule/:id`, `/api/v1/fleet/spec/packs`, and `/api/v1/fleet/spec/packs/:name`. They now return `410 Gone` with a link to the Fleet 5 migration guide. The v1-only pack routes that shared paths with the report-backed schedule endpoints were also removed: `GET /api/v1/fleet/schedule/:id` returns 404 (405 on `2022-04` and later), and `POST /api/v1/fleet/schedule`, `PATCH /api/v1/fleet/schedule/:id`, and `DELETE /api/v1/fleet/schedule/:id` return 404.
- **Breaking change:** Removed the `packs` field from host details, My device, and report API responses.
- **Breaking change:** Removed `fleetctl get packs` and `fleetctl upgrade-packs`. They now fail with a link to the Fleet 5 migration guide, and `fleetctl apply` rejects files that contain a `kind: pack` spec the same way.
- Removed the hidden packs pages in the UI. `/packs` URLs now show the 404 page.
